It is Sunday evening, and I start a video call with my family in Mexico.
The screen lights up, and I can see all of them.
The time difference is quite big.
Here in Denmark, it is eight o'clock in the evening.
But for my parents, Sofía, and Diego, it is only one o'clock in the afternoon.
"Hi Maya!" my dad says and waves.
Suddenly our dog Lola barks at the camera.
Diego laughs and lifts her up so I can see her.
It is lovely to see my family.
I am very happy because we often talk together.
